     "text": "```python\nclass NearestNeighbors:\n    \"\"\"\n    A Nearest Neighbors classifier that implements the k-Nearest Neighbors algorithm.\n    This class follows the coding conventions and guidelines set by SYNERGY, including\n    consistent naming, clear documentation, and maintainable code structure.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, n_neighbors=5):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initialize the Nearest Neighbors classifier.\n\n        Parameters:\n        n_neighbors (int): The number of neighbors to consider when making a prediction.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.n_neighbors = n_neighbors\n        self._X_train = None\n        self._y_train = None\n\n    def fit(self, X, y):\n        \"\"\"\n        Train the classifier on the given training data.\n\n        Parameters:\n        X (array-like): The training data, shape (n_samples, n_features).\n        y (array-like): The target labels for the training data, shape (n_samples,).\n\n        Returns:\n        self: The fitted classifier.\n        \"\"\"\n        self._X_train = X\n        self._y_train = y\n        return self\n\n    def predict(self, X):\n        \"\"\"\n        Predict the class labels for the given test data.\n\n        Parameters:\n        X (array-like): The test data, shape (n_samples, n_features).\n\n        Returns:\n        predictions (array-like): The predicted class labels for the test data.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Calculate the distances between the test samples and all training samples\n        distances = np.sqrt(np.sum((X - self._X_train) ** 2, axis=1))\n        \n        # Sort the distances and get the indices of the nearest neighbors\n        sorted_indices = np.argsort(distances)\n        \n        # Get the labels of the nearest neighbors\n        neighbors_labels = self._y_train[sorted_indices[:self.n_neighbors]]\n        \n        # Return the majority vote among the nearest neighbors\n        return np.bincount(neighbors_labels).argmax()\n```\n\n### Key Points Followed:\n- **Naming Conventions**: \n  - Class name is `NearestNeighbors` (PascalCase).\n  - Method names are in `snake_case` (`fit`, `predict`).\n  - Parameters are named with descriptive names (`X`, `y`, `n_neighbors`).\n- **Documentation**: \n  - Each method has a docstring explaining its purpose, parameters, and return value.\n  - The class docstring provides an overview of the class and its purpose.\n- **Consistency**: \n  - The class follows",
